<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aizu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aizu is the western part of Fukushima Prefecture in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, a mountain basin centred on the castle town of Aizuwakamatsu. It was fought over by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashina-clan">Ashina</a>, Date and other clans in the 16th century and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a> formed a strong domain loyal to the Tokugawa <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shoguns</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boshin-war">Boshin War</a> of 1868 its castle withstood a month-long siege by the forces of the new Meiji government before surrendering.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aizu.jpg" alt="Aizu" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Σ64 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aizuwakamatsu_Castle_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
